> [1] 93.6
> > round(93.75,1)
> [1] 93.8
> > round(93.85,1)
> [1] 93.8
> > round(93.95,1)
> [1] 94
> 
> It seems that if the 1st decimal place is even, then it does not round
> correctly.

What happens here depends on the version of S-PLUS and possibly the
platform.  What then is the correct answer, and who says so?  The results
you give indicate a very sensible round-to-even rule that avoids the
biases in always rounding 0.5 up or always down.  Try reading the help
page (always a good idea before posting)

       When rounding off a 5, the two common conventions are  to:
       1)  go  to  the higher number, or 2) go to the even digit.
       The round function obeys convention 2, so round(2.5) is  2
       and  round(3.5) is 4. The rounding mechanism for signif is
       machine dependent, but most machines will use  the  "round
       to even" rule.

Interestingly, S-PLUS 5.0r3 says that too but

> round(2.5)
[1] 3

and that _is_ a bug, unlike any of yours.

