>> round(93.65,1)
>[1] 93.6
>> round(93.75,1)
>[1] 93.8
>> round(93.85,1)
>[1] 93.8
>> round(93.95,1)
>[1] 94
>
>It seems that if the 1st decimal place is even, then it does not round
>correctly.
>

on the contrary, this is a standard "round-to-even" protocol.
this randomizes the roundoff error in long sequences of calculations,
avoiding the bias inherent in truncation, "round down", and "round up".
