On Wed, 16 Dec 1998, Pintilie, Melania wrote:

> Does anyone know why the survfit function seems to give the output
> differently ordered for 2 seemingly comparable variables?

An important point here is that your example is not the output from
survfit, it is the output produced by print.survfit.  And print.survfit
orders the strata in the order they appear in the file, which is 1,2 in
your first example and 2,1 in the second.  In print.survfit you will find
the line

                for(i in unique(stemp)) {

which you can alter to 

                for(i in sort(unique(stemp))) {

to get the strata in the order of their levels.

[Example deleted]

> This is important when one wants to use the outut of survfit to plot the
> survival curves.

But the problem is not in the output of survfit!  So you need to make the 
same alteration in plot.survfit before plotting, or be aware of the rule
(levels in order in file) in constructing captions/legends.

