Subject: [S] Negative Time Values
Message-ID: <s678ff43.064@amrcorp.com>

** High Priority **

In the transportation industry we do a lot of analysis on time variables. When
comparing the times of actual events to scheduled events we often compute
negative time values. For example, if a flight arrives earlier than scheduled,
the deviation from the scheduled time is negative. If it is late, the deviation
is a positive value. SAS handles the situation well. A common exercise for us
is to simply examine the descriptive statistics on performance populations and
to plot the histograms. When we import negative time values into S-PLUS the
program assigns NAs. Anybody have any suggestions on how we should best handle
these?

