   From the "Changelog" file for the survival package:

2/8/97: Repair minor bug found by Doug McManus.  If x was a factor, then
survfit(Surv(time, status) ~x) would always draw the curves in alphabetical
order, even if that was not the order of the levels.  (The curves were
numerically correct, however).  Now they are drawn in the proper order.

   This repair is part of version 5 of Splus, and it fixes the problem
reported by Melania Pintilie.  Her cateogories were created by "cut",
whose levels are in the right order, but after sorting were not, i.e.,
" 0..." comes before "-1..." in sort order.

