Hello,
my question I posted recently on the data export problem in SPLUS 
4.5. is almost solved:

Normally, I export data as dbf and import data then in Visual FoxPro 
(5). Im general, I find this very robust and this never causes any 
trouble (by the way, I appreciate the FoxPro import feature in SPLUS 
4.5 !).

I wanted to get predicted data from log. regression into FoxPro.
The SPLUS 4.5 data, exported as dbf, and then imported into FoxPro, 
created wrong numbers (I noted they were very close to the ones I 
expected: due to rounding!), and data gaps (when I click on them in 
FoxPro, or set less decimal positions in FoxPro they do show up!). I 
"fixed" this problem by setting the "Line length" in the options of 
data export GUI in SPLUS 4.5.

Still, I think that the options window of the data export in 
SPLUS 4.5 needs to be adjusted and more meaningful to the specific 
export format, e.g. a "delimiter" field in a dbf format is 
unnecessary!

